<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">English Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1642">1642</a>–<a href="/years/1651">1651</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The English Civil War was a series of wars from 1642 to 1651 between the supporters of King Charles I and of Parliament, part of the wider <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-three-kingdoms">Wars of the Three Kingdoms</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and Ireland. Parliament's victory led to the trial and execution of Charles I in 1649, the abolition of the monarchy and the rule of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver Cromwell</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuart-restoration">Restoration of 1660</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/english-civil-war.jpg" alt="English Civil War" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Naseby,_hand-coloured_copper_engraving.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
